From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: cavium: add octeon_pip

Backport to 6.18 of the octeon_pip series prepared for net-next and not
posted yet (16 patches, branch octeon-pip-rfc-v1 of
https://github.com/spolack/linux, 90eb1fd75d25 on net-next
98c2ad4f5d80), squashed into one patch: the driver for the Ethernet
ports behind the PIP/IPD and PKO units of OCTEON, OCTEON+, OCTEON II and
the CN70XX/CN71XX, with phylink and the SGMII/QSGMII/1000BASE-X PCS,
the RGMII/GMII/XAUI ports, a receive group per CPU, transmit completions
in the receive polls, page_pool buffers, XDP (multi-buffer), ethtool and
debugfs. Each SGMII PCS is powered down for 25 ms and up again once at
probe, which QCA8033 PHYs and QCA833x switches need after a warm reset
(what 702-qca833x-force-pcs-reset.patch does for the staging driver).
It replaces the staging driver octeon-ethernet (the two are exclusive in
Kconfig).

Contents: drivers/net/ethernet/cavium/octeon/octeon_pip*, the
OCTEON_PIP_ETHERNET Kconfig entry and Makefile lines, the binding
converted to DT schema (cavium,octeon-3860-pip.yaml, replacing
cavium-pip.txt) and the driver document. MAINTAINERS is left out.

The ports are named eth%d; OpenWrt renames them from the DT property
openwrt,netdev-name (lib/preinit/04_set_netdev_label), through the
net device's of_node the driver sets.

6.18 adaptations: none. The 16 patches apply to 6.18.55 (with the
OpenWrt octeon patches below this one) without changes, and the driver
builds warning-free (also with W=1); the code is byte-identical to the
series. Only the context of the networking document index differs
(Documentation/networking/device_drivers/ethernet/index.rst, fuzz 2).
Kernel behaviour the driver sees differently on 6.18, without a source
change: napi_consume_skb() frees a completed skb on the completing CPU
(7.x defers it to the allocating CPU), netif_queue_set_napi() and
netif_set_real_num_tx_queues() assert the same locks under their 6.18
names, and phylink carries OpenWrt's PCS-provider patches (unused here:
the driver selects its PCS with mac_select_pcs).

Signed-off-by: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
